@startuml receive-accelerator-production-lifecycle
skinparam backgroundColor #F7FAFC
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #334155
  FontColor #0F172A
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  StartColor #334155
  EndColor #334155
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #334155
  FontColor #0F172A
}

state "Absent" as Absent #F1F5F9
Absent : receive_index = None and no build marker;
Absent : readers get Fallback(Absent)

state "Building" as Building #FEF3C7
Building : receive_build = Some(base), where
Building : base = ReceiveBuildBase(revision, loads);
Building : readers get Fallback(Building)

state "Coherent" as Coherent #DCFCE7
Coherent : receive_index = Some(index), maintained in
Coherent : the same write lock as each mutation;
Coherent : receive_handle() pairs it with <latex>(\gamma, \sigma)</latex>

state "Locked rebuild" as Locked #E0E7FF
Locked : rebuild_receive_index_locked() under the
Locked : write lock clears the marker and runs
Locked : rebuild_receive_index() in place

state finish <<choice>>
state maintain <<choice>>

[*] --> Absent : from_snapshot() or a fresh state:\n<latex>\sigma = \gamma</latex>, one fresh base epoch
Absent --> Building : rebuild_receive_accelerator():\nbegin_receive_build() stores the marker\nand clones the continuation store
Building --> finish : build_receive_index() on the\ndetached snapshot, outside the lock
finish -[#15803D]-> Coherent : finish_receive_build(): the marker is still open,\nthe same revision, the same loads (D4),\nno index, and the build is Ok;\nthen publish_receive_index()
finish -[#B91C1C,dashed]-> Locked : refused: a token or loads moved,\nthe marker is gone, or the build failed
Coherent --> Locked : rebuild_receive_accelerator() when\nbegin_receive_build() returns None
Locked --> Coherent : Ok
Locked --> Absent : Err
Coherent --> maintain : set_group, put_prepared,\nremove_path or install
maintain -[#15803D]-> Coherent : support of the group (before, after):\n(false, true) insert_group,\n(true, false) remove_group,\notherwise unchanged
maintain -[#B91C1C,dashed]-> Absent : maintenance fault: insert_group or\nremove_group fails, receive_index = None
Coherent -[#B91C1C]-> Absent : clear() or set_state()
Building -[#B91C1C]-> Absent : clear() or set_state()\ndrops the marker

note left of Coherent #FFEDD5
  <b><latex>\sigma</latex> bump (D1)</b>
  put_continuation (when inserted), install_continuation and
  remove_continuation (when removed) call bump_continuation_revision():
  one fresh ContinuationEpoch becomes the group epoch in
  continuation_epochs, and <latex>\sigma</latex> = continuation_store_epoch
  takes the same allocation. The index is maintained in
  the same write lock, so the store stays Coherent;
  a handle taken earlier: token_class answers Stale.
end note

note right of Absent #FEE2E2
  <b><latex>\gamma</latex> bump</b>
  clear() calls bump_continuation_generation(): a fresh
  continuation_base_epoch <latex>\gamma</latex>, then <latex>\sigma = \gamma</latex> and an
  empty continuation_epochs; RSpaceContinuationStore::clear()
  drops the index. set_state() rebuilds the whole state with
  from_snapshot(), which also issues a fresh <latex>\gamma = \sigma</latex>.
  A handle taken earlier: token_class answers Foreign.
end note

note right of Building #EDE9FE
  <b>History load: no token moves</b>
  get_continuations_versioned() calls set_group(), and
  count_load() increments loads: a build opened before
  the load is refused (D4), so a published index never
  lacks a loaded group. A handle taken before the load
  answers Incomplete for the loaded group (J2 or J3).
end note

legend right
  |= Color |= Meaning |
  |<#F1F5F9> slate | Absent: no published index |
  |<#FEF3C7> amber | Building: a marker is open, readers fall back |
  |<#DCFCE7> green | Coherent: the store's published index, coherent with its live scope |
  |<#E0E7FF> indigo | rebuild in place under the write lock |
  |<#FFEDD5> orange | a <latex>\sigma</latex> bump: earlier handles become Stale |
  |<#FEE2E2> red | a <latex>\gamma</latex> bump: earlier handles become Foreign |
  |<#EDE9FE> violet | a history load: earlier handles answer Incomplete for it |
  | green arrow | publication or maintenance that keeps the index |
  | red arrow | the index or the marker is dropped |
  | red dashed arrow | a refused build or a maintenance fault |
endlegend
@enduml
